 "reading": "The card's primary estimator family is undefined on 9.8-15.1% of its own population: P2 == 0 for 126/1288, 128/1264 and 190/1260 present descending cells, and those cells are systematically LOW out-mass, so the log-log fit is a regression on a sample selected on its own outcome. The registered FIT-UNMEASURABLE escape therefore fired correctly. The exclusion-free instrument is the RANK-BASED neutralising exponent, which is defined on the whole population because a zero numerator gives R_k == 0 at every k. Report k_NEUT (full) as the mass-neutral exponent, k_NEUT (subpopulation) and the three regression estimators as outcome-selected companions, and every residual rho against its COMPONENT-SHUFFLED spurious baseline rather than against zero (Pearson 1897).",
 "limitations": [
  "POST-HOC and UNREGISTERED: no branch, no bar, no prediction. The parent's K_DEGENERATE stands exactly as measured.",
  "k_NEUT is a DESCRIPTIVE reparametrisation that zeroes a rank correlation; it is not a better model of the biology.",
  "The zeros are tied at the bottom of R_k at every k, so k_NEUT is determined entirely by the non-zero cells' ORDERING against m_out -- the zeros contribute rank mass, not slope information.",
  "Three substrates sharing a graph are not three independent replications; one depth, one weighting, no dynamics.",
  "Both actors' percentiles are DESCRIPTIONS OF A SELECTED CELL (Kriegeskorte 2009)."
 ],
